Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:26:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] docs: one writer per unpacked image, and shared host
 resources

On a host where several projects run as the same user, $HOME and therefore
$HOME/sage-image/rootfs is one physical tree. Say so, name the project that owns
writes to it, and give the read-only stamps a consumer reads instead of running
its own build into the same tree; two projects building there would race on one
.lake/build and one site-packages. Note that cgroups are per project while the
memory and CPUs are the host's, and that there is no swap, so parallel long
builds across projects compete rather than queue.
